Wishless, genoless, and polypileless are the easiest of the conducts,
sure, but they're still more impressive than a plain, conductless
ascension.  

Genoless is pretty trivial, considering the only truly dangerous and
genocidable monsters are 'L's and 'h's and neither of those are
significant problems if you're prepared.  

Wishless can be as easy or difficult as you want to make it.  I've had
some hellishly difficult wishless ascensions simply because I forged on
through the dungeon without waiting around to get stuff like speed
boots, DSM, reflection, MR, BoH, etc...  However, those might have been
easy games if I had waited around for better equipment.  My thinking is
that conducts are supposed to be _hard_, not just inconvenient, so
waiting around to get a perfect AK without wishes is an exercise in
patience, not skill.  

And of course, polypileless can be an important addition, since a
wishless game with lots of polypiling isn't significantly more difficult
than a game with bunches of wishes.  

Anyway, any conduct is good.  I feel that an ascension is always better
than a non-ascension and an ascension with conducts is always better
than a conductless one.  

